# Package activation examples

This package (`@gkgo/pi-packages`) is runtime-disabled by default. Use `pi config` to select extensions interactively. For a deterministic settings-file activation, list the extension directory directly in Pi's global (`~/.pi/agent/settings.json`) or trusted project (`.pi/settings.json`) `extensions` array.

## Enable one extension (then opt it in at runtime)

Replace `/path/to/pi-packages` with the installed package directory. For npm and git packages, this is the installed `@gkgo/pi-packages` directory shown by `pi list`/`pi config`, not the source specifier.

```json
{
  "extensions": ["/path/to/pi-packages/dist/file-guard"]
}
```

Choose one of these exact paths:

- `dist/file-guard/index.js`
- `dist/workers/index.js`
- `dist/thinking-compression/index.js`
- `dist/gondolin/index.js` (requires this package's `node_modules` for the external `@earendil-works/gondolin` dependency)

The `dist/` bundles are self-contained: their non-Pi dependencies are inlined, so they load even when the package's `node_modules` is cleared. The TypeScript sources under `extensions/` are for development and require the package's `node_modules` to be installed.

## Enable all bundled extensions (then opt each in at runtime)

```json
{
  "extensions": [
    "/path/to/pi-packages/dist/file-guard",
    "/path/to/pi-packages/dist/workers",
    "/path/to/pi-packages/dist/thinking-compression",
    "/path/to/pi-packages/dist/gondolin"
  ]
}
```

The extension-specific runtime opt-ins must also be configured: enable File Guard in its config/environment, set `enabled: true` in `.pi/workers.json`, and set `enabled: true` in Gondolin Sandbox configuration (see [`gondolin.json.example`](gondolin.json.example)). MCP servers are Pi's built-in `mcp.json` concern (see [`mcp.json.example`](mcp.json.example)), not a bundled extension.